_:n4b0e586f6bfe48d0be092ebf6a59ba60xb0	http://schema.org/description	"Welcome to the DoubleTree by Hilton Hotel Coventry Building Society Arena. This impressive hotel enjoys a prime location in The Coventry Building Society Arena, home of Premiership Rugby Club Wasps and Coventry City FC. The Coventry Building Society Arena is also host to business, entertainment and sporting events, as well as the Grosvenor G Casino Coventry. Connect easily with three train stations within eight miles and reach Birmingham International Airport in 20 minutes. Your stay begins with a freshly baked chocolate chip cookie at check-in. Each guest room at our DoubleTree by Hilton hotel features Wi-Fi access, a 42-inch or 47-inch HDTV and tea - coffee facilities. Some guest rooms boast stadium pitch views. Corporate guests will appreciate the sleek workspace and evening room service. Choose a suite for separate living and dining areas. Enjoy breakfast in our stylish restaurant and keep up with the latest news and sports in The Anecdote Sports Bar. The Anecdote offers an a la carte menu and is perfect for a quick lunch or snack. It has a fully stocked bas with draught and bottled beers, wines and spirits. Re-energize after a busy day in our fitness center with Precor equipment. Guests can enjoy access to a wealth of event space at The Coventry Building Society Arena, which Hosts up to 7,000 guests in the 6,000 sq. mt. Exhibition Hall. Coventry Building Society Arena hosts hundreds of exhibitions and conferences every year, with the onsite DoubleTree by Hilton Hotel providing convenient accommodation for delegates. Coventry Building Society Arena is synonymous with music, and many of the biggest acts in the world have performed here, including the Killers, Spice girls, Bon Jovi and Take That. The Arena also houses an onsite railway station which services links delivered by West Midlands Trains. The city of Coventry is approximately a 20-minute walk from the DoubleTree by Hilton Hotel at Coventry Building Society Arena."
