_:n022ea59861e04699a1f8ccc94e608b14xb0	http://schema.org/description	"This is El Gouna in Egypt. Explore the shores of the Red Sea from Casa Cook's latest hideaway. Opening in November 2019, the newly built 5 star hotel is the fifth of Thomas Cook's award-winning collection of boutique hotels, designed with the postmodern family in mind.\n \nFlanked by palms and perched amidst the desert mountains, the 100-room family-friendly hotel is the perfect base to relax and unwind. The rugged landscape is juxtaposed with contemporary Arabic architecture and green gardens– your own secluded settlement, with sweeping azure vistas of the Red Sea. \n \nSpend your days by the pool, indulging at the spa, exploring archaeological treasures or experiencing the world-class diving and kitesurfing on offer. The rooms – ranging from Standard Rooms to Villas – feel earthy and private, like a home away from home. Each room features an own private terrace, while the Premium Roof Terrace rooms boast expansive sunset views. Shades of orange and red offset the darker nuances of green and blue, while raw wooden furnishings and tarnished ceramics create a sense of pared back luxury. Décor is simple and chic, complimented with rattan interiors and neutral linens. Junior suites share a pool per unit of 2 suites, whereas villas enjoy a fully private pool for full family intimacy. This is El Gouna in Egypt. Explore the shores of the Red Sea from Casa Cook's latest hideaway. Opening in november 2019, the newly built 5 star hotel is the fifth of Thomas Cook's award-winning collection of boutique hotels, designed with the postmodern family in mind.\n \nFlanked by palms and perched amidst the desert mountains, the 100-room family-friendly hotel is the perfect base to relax and unwind. The rugged landscape is juxtaposed with contemporary Arabic architecture and green gardens– your own secluded settlement, with sweeping azure vistas of the Red Sea."
