_:n12bb2e57b1254f5c9ed6a4a3c7be0fa6xb0	http://schema.org/description	"Located in the picture-perfect Red Sea resort of Hurghada, this all-inclusive hotel flaunts a host of swanky facilities. And nothing screams luxury like a far-stretching complex made up of seven pools, eight waterslides and seven eateries. But most importantly, you can take advantage of Egypt’s underwater allures with a private beach and diving centre at your disposal. \r\n\r\nAll rooms are kitted out with comfy furnishings and ample space to unwind after a day in Hurghada’s blazing heat. Interiors reflect traditional Egyptian decor with tiled floors, wooden fixtures and beautifully patterned rugs. Facilities-wise, all the essentials are covered including air-conditioning, a TV, hairdryer, mini bar, safe and balcony/terrace. \r\n\r\nDepending on what you’re after, guests can opt for a double room, junior suite or family-sized accommodation. Or, how about waking up to the pool at your feet? Thanks to the hotel’s swim-up option you could upgrade to your very own water oasis. \r\n\r\nIf you’re seeking ample choice, you’ve come to the right place. There are two main restaurants whipping up international buffet spreads morning, noon and evening. Not forgetting the five a la cartes specialising in Italian, Mongolian, Asian, Japanese and seafood dishes. And when you just fancy a light bite, there’s a snack shack on hand serving hot dogs and burgers. Grab yourself a cocktail from one of its eight drinking spots including a venue on the beach. Or, head over to  the Oriental tent for a cup of coffee and Shisha. \r\n\r\nGuests can dine at the hotel’s a la carte restaurants twice per week for free, any visits after this will be chargeable. And be sure to book in advance to avoid any disappointment. \r\n\r\nThis hotel has really gone above and beyond when it comes to facilities, and its waterpark takes the crown. Home to the largest aquapark in the whole of Hurghada, it’s an adrenaline-junkies’ paradise. Feel the thrill as you plunge down vertical drops, float its rafting river and take on the rapid wave pool. Your tiny travellers also get their own pool complete with a pirate ship and splash zones. \r\n\r\nAway from the waterpark madness, there’s also plenty of relaxing pool areas where you can unwind in tranquil surroundings. Or, you can always head to the spa where a full body scrub and Turkish bath are waiting. When the sun goes down, the resort comes alive with mini disco parties for the kids, live music and dance performances. \r\n\r\nFancy a break from the sunshine? Then, visit the nearby Senzo Mall. Here you can shop for jewellery, footwear and fashion, grab a coffee and let the kids have fun on arcade style games. Or, check out Hurghada Marina Boulevard! It’s a bustling area both day and night, with a selection of bars and restaurants serving local delicacies, such as camel steaks, as well as international cuisine. And you can’t visit Hurghada without diving into the depths of its coral reefs. It’s home to some of the best diving spots in the world, including the natural park at Giftun Island where you’ll spot turtles, fish and dolphins!"
